      "id": "PES-HESSIAN-CONSTRAINT",
      "status": "confirmed mathematical limitation",
      "locator": "PES main PDF pp.4–5, C1.1/C1.2 and sampled off-diagonal substitution",
      "observation": "Negative Hessian diagonal entries imply negative definiteness for a diagonal Hessian, but not with arbitrary fixed nonzero off-diagonals. A negative-definite sampled Hessian [[-3,2],[2,-3]] supplies off-diagonal 2; the allowed replacement [[-1,2],[2,-1]] has eigenvalues 1,-3. Gaussian EP approximations also do not retain hard sign support exactly.",
      "handling": "Describe the local constraints as approximation factors, not a certificate that the conditioned point is a local or global maximum."
    },
    {
      "id": "PES-SUPP-BLOCK-ORDER",
      "status": "confirmed printed discrepancy with bounded exact witness",
      "locator": "Supplement B.1 PDF p.2 / printed p.11; B.3 PDF pp.3–4 / printed pp.12–13",
      "observation": "K is defined on [z;c] and K_dagger against [z;c], but the displayed prediction uses [c;tilde_m] and W=diag(0,tilde_V), consistent instead with [c;z].",
      "handling": "The Gaussian integral in Eq.12 is unambiguous. For stated [z;c] ordering, use compatible vector [tilde_m;c] and noise block diag(tilde_V,0), or reorder every matrix consistently. The constructed witness gives mean/variance 4,2/3 with consistent ordering versus 9,0 literally. This is curator algebra, not an author erratum."
    },
