      "id": "PES-RANDOM-FEATURE-EXACTNESS",
      "status": "scope qualification",
      "locator": "PES Section 2.1 p.3 and Supplement A PDF pp.1–2 / printed pp.10–11",
      "observation": "Feature inner products average to the kernel under the spectral construction, but finite-feature posterior inference is approximate. The supplement wording about equivalence must not be read as commuting expectations through a matrix inverse.",
      "handling": "For fixed features the Bayesian linear model is exactly a GP with that finite-rank feature kernel. Unbiased feature kernels do not give the exact original GP posterior; a scalar random covariance example yields average posterior variance 5/8 versus 2/3 at the averaged kernel."
    },
    {
      "id": "PES-HYPERPARAMETER-OBJECTIVE",
      "status": "scope qualification",
      "locator": "PES Section 2.3 p.5, Eq.10 and Algorithm 2 p.2",
      "observation": "The implemented average is over conditional fixed-hyperparameter information approximations. It is not generally identical to I(x_star;y|D) under the fully marginalized model. Eq.10 leaves sigma squared unindexed even though psi includes the noise variance.",
      "handling": "State E_psi[I(x_star;y|D,x,psi)] as the conditional-acquisition average, with each variance/noise term belonging to its hyperparameter draw. A fair-bit XOR example gives mean conditional MI log(2) but marginal MI zero. Do not claim the source evaluates exact fully marginalized optimizer entropy."
    },
    {
      "id": "ES-EI-SIGN",
      "status": "confirmed printed comparator discrepancy retained from shortlist",
      "locator": "ES PDF p.4 / printed p.1812, Section 1.1.3",
      "observation": "The EI expectation uses min{0,eta-f}, while its displayed closed form is the nonnegative-improvement expression.",
      "handling": "This comparator formula does not define ES. Its PI/EI representer-point proposal discussion does not make ES the EI acquisition method."
