      "observation": "The model defines y=f(x)+epsilon, but the derivation calls p(y|D,x) Gaussian with latent variance kt(x,x) and requires y<m. With nonzero observation noise the predictive variance includes sigma_noise^2 and observations may exceed the latent maximum.",
      "handling": "Describe Eq6 as the original latent/local-truncation acquisition approximation, not exact noisy mutual information. Do not silently insert noise into a formula and claim it is the original method."
